+# Plan: safe category deletion
+
+1. Update `CategoryServiceImpl.delete` to resolve the root in the owning store, collect the root and all descendants, load products attached to any affected category, remove only those category links from each product, and update/flush the products. Never call `ProductService.delete` from category deletion.
+2. Delete the affected category subtree after the join-table links are removed, using the existing category cascade where safe and explicitly deleting descendants if needed so no child category remains.
+3. Update `CategoryFacadeImpl.deleteCategory(Long, MerchantStore)` to use the store-scoped category lookup and throw `ResourceNotFoundException` for a missing id.
+4. Add focused regression coverage for preserving products and their non-deleted category links, deleting descendants, returning 404 for deleted/missing categories, and returning no products for the deleted category. Reuse existing integration test support and avoid changing cart/order data.
+5. Run formatting/compile checks as applicable, the focused category tests, and the Maven test/build command for the affected modules; inspect failures and adjust only the implementation or tests required by this behavior.
